            <ArticleTitle>CT-guided stereotactic antero-medial pulvinotomy and centromedian-parafascicular thalamotomy for intractable malignant pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>195-200</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A quick and safe CT image-guided stereotactic thalamotomy technique that has proved ideal for alleviating medically refractory intractable pain due to malignant disease is described. A simple method of deriving cartesian coordinates for target points that facilitates functional neurosurgery using CT images and the Brown-Roberts-Wells stereotactic system is also described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
